    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38932" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prō-porro</span></b> , adv. (Lucretian).
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>furthermore</i>, <i>moreover</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">et, sibi proporro quae sint primordia,
					quaerunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					2, 979</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4, 890</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">5, 312</span></i>; Lucil.
			ap. <i><span class="en">Non. p. 140,
			13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in gen., <i>altogether</i>, <i>utterly</i>, <i>wholly</i>, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 3, 275</span></i>; <i><span class="en">281</span></i>.</div>
